    "note": "Captured in-container at measure time. /proc/loadavg inside the container is normally the HOST's (containers share the kernel), and Linux counts processes blocked on I/O (I/O-wait) toward load average, so a high loadavg can appear even when the CPU is idle; cpu_idle_pct = (idle+iowait)/total from /proc/stat is recorded alongside so the two can be read together. Each metric's _min is the least-contended run's estimate, and the _min-vs-median gap is the contention signal."
